<title>UK: Ashtead to replace London Elec in FTSE 250.</title>
<headline>Ashtead to replace London Elec in FTSE 250.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>FTSE actuaries said on Monday that plant machinery hire company Ashtead Group Plc had replaced regional electricity company London Electricity Plc in the FTSE 250 Index.</p>
<p>Ashtead's inclusion in the index, which took effect after Monday's close of business, follows the purchase of London Electricity by U.S. utility group Entergy Corporation.</p>
<p>--London newsroom  + 44 171 5424366</p>
